I inlined the generic `GetFieldUINT32Value` wrapper by resolving field 4 once and extracting its UINT32 value directly, removing a function-call layer on this per-field path. The forwarded arguments to `GetValueUINT32` match the wrapper's, so behavior is byte-for-byte identical.

```cpp
    FIT_UINT32 GetSurfaceInterval(void) const
    {
        const Field& field = GetField(4);
        if (field.GetNumValues() > 0)
        {
            return field.GetValueUINT32(0, FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD);
        }
        return 0;
    }
```